{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/968128-massachusett-magi","id":968128,"title":"Massachusett Magi","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-12T13:57:07-07:00","id":968128,"title":"Massachusett Magi","content":"This comes off the back of the First and Indigenous Peoples in CoD thread. Personally I really like the Boston Unveiled setting, but I feels like it lacks a degree of historical depth. Like, when running games set in Britain, there's at least two thousand years of relatively continuous culture. I could give the local Mysterium an actual Mithraeum becuase the city I set the game in had a real life Mithras cult.<br /> <br /> In Boston however everything seems to have been done post-colonisation, There's very little feeling of history beyond that.There are references to the local tribes having Awakened cultures of their own, and little bits and pieces here and there like the Chariot of Epona supposedly incorporating Native American lore into their practices, but it doesn't really detail them at all. A major trope of Awakening is delving into the past in search of mysteries, but I can't really do that if I have no idea what the historical people actually believed.<br /> <br /> So, I've been trying to research the Native Peoples of the Boston area, with an eye towards working out some kind of rough Great Cult mythos for the Awakened of the Massachusett before the colony. I've come across a few bits, but it's pretty hard going. I've actually been wondering about cannibalising Doubting Souls for the Keepers of the Weave who could easily pass as a Mysterium-esque group.<br /> <br /> Does anyone else have any ideas?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T14:52:16-07:00","id":968155,"title":"","content":"While it is not proper Native American it has some aboriginal vibes you could get inspiration from: <br /> Hellblazer #89 <a href=\"http://hellblazer.wikia.com/wiki/Hellblazer_issue_89\" target=\"_blank\">http://hellblazer.wikia.com/wiki/Hellblazer_issue_89</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6169-shadowjim12","name":"Shadowjim12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T15:28:21-07:00","id":968182,"title":"","content":"I haven't read Boston Unveiled in some time, and don't currently have the book handy, but wasn't the reason for the post-colonial feel because the European mages wiped-put, subjugated or drove-off the natives in a manner similar to their Sleeper brethren?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T15:54:32-07:00","id":968207,"title":"","content":"Didn't it say that the native Awakened were wiped out when the original European Mages cast a spell that rewrote reality?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T16:04:09-07:00","id":968219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/968128-massachusett-magi?p=968182#post968182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't read Boston Unveiled in some time, and don't currently have the book handy, but wasn't the reason for the post-colonial feel because the European mages wiped-put, subjugated or drove-off the natives in a manner similar to their Sleeper brethren?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, kinda. The magi themselves were largely driven off, but there are references to the Stone Assembly and Chariot of Epona collecting native lore and objects. For the Awakened that kind of knowledge has real value no matter the source. The Mysterium book especially makes the point that European Magi have had a tendency to walk off with other peoples stuff; the magical knowledge has value that the people themselves don't.<br /> <br /> I agree the post-colonial feel is quite important to the setting, but I feel like it could be emphasised a bit more. As it stands it just glanced over. Like, it mentions the Assembly gathering up native objects... but doesn't say what kinds of things those would be. To me that suggests imbued items and magical tools but... I honestly don't really know what kind of items the Native people in the area would have had.<br /> <br /> There's also the issue of ancient mage sites. They're a pretty common staple of Mage, but in Boston there's seven thousand years worth of Awakened culture to look through as compared to 500 years of colonial history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T16:11:11-07:00","id":968223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/968128-massachusett-magi?p=968207#post968207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't it say that the native Awakened were wiped out when the original European Mages cast a spell that rewrote reality?</div> </div> </div> </div>I did wonder about that though I think it's referring to the specific group that the Chariot was in conflict with. I feel if it had meant all native magi, it'd have made a bigger deal out of that. But that is an interesting idea, it does kinda parrallel the importation of disease from Europe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T02:42:50-07:00","id":970588,"title":"","content":"I made from natives legends <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=827351#post827351\">my own take on the 'Secret Concord'</a> of Boston, to make it more open ended Mystery to be used.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:24px\"><b>Great Mystery of New England \u2013 Spirit of Land</b></span><br /> There are forces in New England lands. Secret whispers between the sights of wind. The sounds of running river are the same as rhythms of Supernal incantations. Lines of power are crossing land, pointing to forgotten symbols. Immaterial beings are hunting those places for centuries \u2013 and yet they work in to something greater, like common mind. Natives American say this land has its own <i>soul</i>. They may not be wrong\u2026<br /> <br /> From the time first European witches and sorcerers come to the New World, they tried to communicate with this intelligence. It is commonly called \u201eSpirit of Land\u201d \u2013 but Awakened are not sure is it spirit, goetia, powerful ghosts \u2013 or even just some presence they feel when they are alone in the woods. All they want to be study it. And to get the power from it.<br /> <br /> Many attempts on this gone badly \u2013 Spirit, if it\u2019s even exists, is fighting with mages to not get locked up by them. Salem Witch trials are said to be result of first famous attempt. Hubristic Awakened tried to play with forces they could not understood \u2013 and innocent people paid the price. Or at least it\u2019s what Guardians of Veil from New England say.<br /> <br /> Secret Concord from Boston is to be the latest successive attempt on that. Whoever \u2013 no, <i>what</i>ever - is third signer of the document is probably the \u201eThe Spirit of Land\u201d. This is why Ebon Noose and White Putnams so much fortune favors them - the land itself helps them to maintain power. Or so rumors in Awakened circles say.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\"><b>Possible solutions to Mystery:</b></span><ul><li><b><i>Spirit of the Land</i></b> \u2013 Mysterious being most Awakened sought to know in New England <i>is</i> a powerful Shadows spirit of this Lands. It\u2019s Rank 7 being, on par of Wolf gods the werewolf worship or just a bit below ephemeral beings like Sun or Moon. Many wonder how spirit of surrounding can be this powerful and wonder if Atlantean civilizations that left ruins in New England woods have something to do with it. ( See <b>Boston Unveiled</b>, Chapter Four \u201eOff the Map\u201d )</li> </ul><ul><li><b><i>Bound</i></b> <b><i>unbound </i></b>\u2013 Other theory states that this being is Supernal god, thrown into our world when Exarchs took their Thrones. Instead of being bound in some ancient prison, this being freed itself and roam freely the land. It would explained local Seers interest in to phenomena, as one of their most important dogmas it to lock and sentry this kind of beings. It would also clear why some Awakened disappear in the middle of the night when left alone in the woods \u2013 Bound are always hungry for Mana, pouncing on anything that has a greater amount of it in his Pattern. Awakened are then ideal meal.</li> </ul><ul><li><b><i>Prisoner from Abyss </i></b>\u2013 Most disturbing theory is that \u201eSpirit\u201d is powerful Acamoth, abyssal being living in Astral Space. Most seek mages to use their Astral link with Abyss to go over their home they were separated eons ago. But the New England being had somehow evolved and can travel between strata of Astral on its own \u2013 it lies in Anima Mundi most often, leaving imprint on the land and beings in region. Still, it likes to play with Awakened, offering lore and power. For the price.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}